6. Proof-carrier tournament
  scores={'triadic_centers': 2, 'half_center': 4, 'both_center_families': 5, 'mixed_residual': 1, 'AP_mu_sequence': 3, 'colored_resonance_tail': 0}
  score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1}, cycles3=0, sccs=[1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1], Hamiltonian_paths=1, leader=both_center_families

7. Takeaway
  The integer sequence survivor(s)=C(7,s)+C(9,s)-C(5,s) is the exact
  small-part split for the universal denominator-cap skeleton.
  It proves a c/R reservoir for all-odd or 3-free small parts, and
  identifies the mixed parity/triadic residual as the real Diophantine tail.
  This does not finish LRC(14); it makes the remaining proof obligation smaller
  and cleaner: solve the mixed residual by colored resonance / spread recurrence.
